<Routines>
<Routine Name="R1_MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 

====================================================================================================

Sample program for Kinematics SCARA Independent J1J2J3J6 Robot feature, via  MCTO, MCPM programming;
MCTO Target positions are programmed using path positions in the MCPM instruction.

============== MCTO Setup ================

Source Coordinate System = CS_XYZRXRyRz (6 Virtual Axes, Geometry = Cartesian)

Robot Coordinate System = J1J2J3J6 (4 Joint Axes, Geometry = SCARA J1J2J3J6 Independent)   

====================================================================================================

================================================================
Open Trends (under Controller Organizer\Trends) to view the following plots:
1. Cartesian Axes.
2. Joint Axes
3. Rz_Coupling_Effect
4. XY Plot.
5. XZ Plot.
6. YZ Plot

==================================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R2_JogMaster,0)JSR(R3_SCARA_Pick_n_Place,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
==========================

USER SETUP:
Toggle bits from left to right in this Routine or individually from the SCARA_Pick

===========================
1. Start_SCARA_Test

2. Select the Type of MCPM Move: Incremental, Absolute or Work Tool based

3. Start_MCTO : MCTO instruction is used to establish a bidirectional transform that is
 set up between a Cartesian and a robot system with coordinates that are joint axes of a robot. 

4. Robot Configuration: To change the Robot Configuration, select any one of the following Configurations:
SCARA_Config _Righty : Select SCARA Robot as a Righty Configuration 
SCARA_Config _Lefty : Select SCARA Robot as a Lefty Configuration

5. Start_Pick_n_Place.

========================================================

Start_MCTPO_Forward/Start_MCTPO_Inverse: 
MCTPO instruction is used to calculate the position of a point in one coordinate system 
to the equivalent point in a second coordinate system. 
To calculate Cartesian position, select Forward. To calculate Robot joint positions, select Inverse.

============


]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_SCARA_Test)[XIC(MCPM_Incremental_Move) ,XIC(MCPM_Absolute_Move) ,XIC(MCPM_with_WorkTool) ]XIC(Start_MCTO)[XIC(SCARA_Config_RIGHTY) ,XIC(SCARA_Config_LEFTY) ]XIC(Start_Pick_n_Place)[XIC(Start_MCTPO_Forward) ,XIC(Start_MCTPO_Inverse) ]NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Controlled Stop of All Axes and Joints

==================================================]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCS_Cart)XIC(MCS_Robot)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R2_JogMaster" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Use the Motion Axis Jog (MAJ) instruction to move an axis at a constant speed (using MAJ_Master) until a stop is issued.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(MAJ_Control.EN)MAJ(VirtualMaster,MAJ_Control,0,MAJ_Master_Speed,0,100,0,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R3_SCARA_Pick_n_Place" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
===============================================

SCARA Pick n Place Application

=====================================================================



Reset all startup bits, instruction flags and initialize Step
================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(s:fs) ,XIC(Reset_All) ][MOV(-3,Step) ,OTU(Start_Pick_n_Place) ,OTU(SCARA_Config_RIGHTY) OTU(SCARA_Config_LEFTY) ,OTU(Start_MCTO) ,OTU(Start_MCTPO_Forward) OTU(Start_MCTPO_Inverse) ,OTU(Start_SCARA_Test) ,OTU(MCPM_Absolute_Move) OTU(MCPM_Incremental_Move) OTU(MCPM_with_WorkTool) ,OTU(Pick_n_Place_One_Cycle) OTU(Pick_n_Place_Continuous_Cycle) ,CLR(MCTO_Control.FLAGS) CLR(MDCC_Control.FLAGS) ,CLR(MCTPO_Control[0].FLAGS) CLR(MCTPO_Control[1].FLAGS) ,OTU(Reset_All) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear all MCPM Instruction Flags
==================================]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Step,-3)[CLR(MCPM_Control[0].FLAGS) CLR(MCPM_Control[1].FLAGS) CLR(MCPM_Control[2].FLAGS) ,CLR(MCPM_Control[3].FLAGS) CLR(MCPM_Control[4].FLAGS) CLR(MCPM_Control[5].FLAGS) ,CLR(MCPM_Control[6].FLAGS) CLR(MCPM_Control[7].FLAGS) CLR(MCPM_Control[8].FLAGS) ,CLR(MAH_CONTROL[0].FLAGS) CLR(MAH_CONTROL[1].FLAGS) CLR(MAH_CONTROL[2].FLAGS) CLR(MAH_CONTROL[3].FLAGS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Move the Joint Axes to Home or Reference Position using MAH Instruction, before initiating MCTO Instruction
(This bit - Start_SCARA_Test can be toggled here, in case if not done from the R1_MainRoutine)

============================================================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_SCARA_Test)EQU(Step,-3)XIC(Robot.GroupSynced)XIO(Reset_All)[[MAH(J1,MAH_CONTROL[0]) ,MAH(J2,MAH_CONTROL[1]) ,MAH(J3,MAH_CONTROL[2]) ,MAH(J6,MAH_CONTROL[3]) ] ,XIC(J1.AxisHomedStatus) XIC(J2.AxisHomedStatus) XIC(J3.AxisHomedStatus) XIC(J6.AxisHomedStatus) MOV(-2,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Select the Type of MCPM Move: Incremental, Absolute or Work Tool based
(Any one of these bits - MCPM_Incremental_Move, MCPM_Absolute_Move or MCPM_with_WorkTool  can be toggled here, in case if not done from the R1_MainRoutine)

======================================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Step,-2)XIO(Reset_All)[XIC(MCPM_Incremental_Move) COP(SCARA4D_Inc_Path[0],SCARA_Path[0],20) COP(Default_WorkFrame,WorkFrame,1) COP(Default_ToolFrame,ToolFrame,1) OTU(MCPM_Absolute_Move) OTU(MCPM_with_WorkTool) ,XIC(MCPM_Absolute_Move) COP(SCARA4D_Abs_Path[0],SCARA_Path[0],20) COP(Default_WorkFrame,WorkFrame,1) COP(Default_ToolFrame,ToolFrame,1) OTU(MCPM_Incremental_Move) OTU(MCPM_with_WorkTool) ,XIC(MCPM_with_WorkTool) COP(SCARA4D_Work_Tool_Path[0],SCARA_Path[0],20) COP(MCPM_WorkFrame,WorkFrame,1) COP(MCPM_ToolFrame,ToolFrame,1) OTU(MCPM_Incremental_Move) OTU(MCPM_Absolute_Move) ]MOV(-1,Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Enable MCTO followed by Motion Coordinated Master Driven Speed Control for controlling the speed of the "Pick and Place" application through a singular virtual master
(This bit - Start_MCTO can be toggled here, in case if not done from the R1_MainRoutine)


=====================================================================================================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTO)EQU(Step,-1)XIO(Reset_All)[MCTO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,SCARA_Indep_J1J2J3J6,MCTO_Control,WorkFrame,ToolFrame) XIC(MCTO_Control.IP) XIO(MCTO_Control.ER) MDCC(CS_XYZRxRyRz,VirtualMaster,MDCC_Control,Command,1.0) ,XIC(MDCC_Control.IP) MOV(0,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
To change the Robot Configuration, set the appropriate bit (RIGHTY or LEFTY)
(One of these bits - SCARA_Config_RIGHTY OR SCARA_Config_LEFTY can be toggled here, in case if not done from the R1_MainRoutine)

============================================================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SCARA_Config_RIGHTY)ONS(ons1)OTU(SCARA_Config_LEFTY);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SCARA_Config_LEFTY)ONS(ons2)OTU(SCARA_Config_RIGHTY);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[


Joint Moves to Initial Position either as a Righty Config or as a Lefty Config

=========================================================================

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Step,0)XIO(Reset_All)[XIC(SCARA_Config_RIGHTY) [MAM(J1,MAM_Control[0],0,-30,Joint_Axis_Speed[0],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[0],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[0],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) MAM(J2,MAM_Control[1],0,90,Joint_Axis_Speed[1],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[1],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[1],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) ,MAM(J3,MAM_Control[2],0,10,Joint_Axis_Speed[2],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[2],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[2],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) MAM(J6,MAM_Control[3],0,0,Joint_Axis_Speed[3],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[3],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[3],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) ] ,XIC(SCARA_Config_LEFTY) [MAM(J1,MAM_Control[4],0,60,Joint_Axis_Speed[4],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[4],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[4],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) MAM(J2,MAM_Control[5],0,-90,Joint_Axis_Speed[5],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[5],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[5],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) ,MAM(J3,MAM_Control[6],0,10,Joint_Axis_Speed[6],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[6],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[6],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) MAM(J6,MAM_Control[7],0,0,Joint_Axis_Speed[7],0,Joint_Accel_Rate[7],0,Joint_Decel_Rate[7],0,0,100,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) ] ][XIC(MAM_Control[0].PC) XIC(MAM_Control[1].PC) XIC(MAM_Control[2].PC) XIC(MAM_Control[3].PC) ,XIC(MAM_Control[4].PC) XIC(MAM_Control[5].PC) XIC(MAM_Control[6].PC) XIC(MAM_Control[7].PC) ]MOV(1,Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
================ PICK n PLACE Moves  ================


=====================================================

By Default, the Pick and Place Moves are set to Multiple Cycles.
To set to a SingleCycle of Pick and Place Move, Toggle the Pick_n_Place_One_Cycle Bit.
To set to Multiple Cycles of Pick and Place Moves, Toggle the Pick_n_Place_Continuous_Cycle Bit to Unlatch the Pick_n_Place_One_Cycle Bit.

===============================================================================================================]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Pick_n_Place_One_Cycle)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Pick_n_Place_Continuous_Cycle)OTU(Pick_n_Place_One_Cycle)OTU(Pick_n_Place_Continuous_Cycle);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[

Start multi-dimensional coordinated path moves using MCPM Instructions
(This bit - Start_Pick_n_Place can be toggled here, in case if not done from the R1_MainRoutine)


=========================================================================]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.0)XIC(Start_Pick_n_Place)EQU(Step,1)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[0],SCARA_Path[0],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[0].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(2,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.1)EQU(Step,2)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[1],SCARA_Path[1],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[1].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(3,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.2)EQU(Step,3)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[2],SCARA_Path[2],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[2].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(4,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.3)EQU(Step,4)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[3],SCARA_Path[3],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[3].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(5,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.4)EQU(Step,5)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[4],SCARA_Path[4],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[4].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(6,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.5)EQU(Step,6)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[5],SCARA_Path[5],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[5].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(7,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.6)EQU(Step,7)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[6],SCARA_Path[6],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[6].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(8,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.7)EQU(Step,8)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[7],SCARA_Path[7],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[7].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(9,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(stepz.8)EQU(Step,9)XIO(Reset_All)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCPM_Control[8],SCARA_Path[8],1,DynamicDataJoint,0,Immediate Forward Only) ,XIC(MCPM_Control[8].IP) XIO(Pick_n_Place_One_Cycle) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(1,Step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Initiate MCTPO Forward Instruction]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTPO_Forward)COP(SCARA_Indep_J1J2J3J6.ActualPosition[0],MCTPO_Fwd_Input[0],6)MCTPO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,SCARA_Indep_J1J2J3J6,MCTPO_Control[0],WorkFrame,ToolFrame,Forward,MCTPO_Fwd_Input,MCTPO_Fwd_Output,Robot_Config,Turns_Counter[0])OTU(Start_MCTPO_Forward)OTU(Start_MCTPO_Inverse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Initiate MCTPO Inverse Instruction]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTPO_Inverse)COP(CS_XYZRxRyRz.ActualPosition[0],MCTPO_Inv_Input[0],8)MCTPO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,SCARA_Indep_J1J2J3J6,MCTPO_Control[1],WorkFrame,ToolFrame,Inverse,MCTPO_Inv_Input,MCTPO_Inv_Output,Robot_Config,Turns_Counter[0])OTU(Start_MCTPO_Inverse)OTU(Start_MCTPO_Forward);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Joint Command Positions moved to Tags for visualisation purposes, for HMI/SCADA/OPC
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(J1.CommandPosition,J1_Pos)MOV(J2.CommandPosition,J2_Pos)MOV(J3.CommandPosition,J3_Pos)MOV(J6.CommandPosition,J6_Pos);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Controlled Stop of coordinated motion (X, Y, Z, Rx, Ry, Rz) using MCS Instruction]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCS_Cart)EQU(Step,-3)MCS(CS_XYZRxRyRz,MCS_Control[0],Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0)OTU(MCS_Cart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Controlled Stop of Joints (J1, J2, J3, J6) using MCS Instruction]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCS_Robot)EQU(Step,-3)MCS(SCARA_Indep_J1J2J3J6,MCS_Control[1],Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0)OTU(MCS_Robot);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R4_Readme_File" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[(*]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[ /*  ============================================================================= */	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[				  SCARA Independent J1J2J3J6 Robot    ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[ /*  ============================================================================= */	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[This program contains a 4-Axis SCARA Robot demonstrating a simple "Pick and Place" application in XYZ plane.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[It also demonstrates the Speed override functionality (scaling the entire "Pick and Place" dynamics using a single master axis).]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[Motion Groups-> Robot-> Coordinate System Properties: J1J2J3J6]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[Lead Parameter Value is set to 36 coordination units/Rev to show the relationship between the linear and rotational axis on a ball screw. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[Note: When the Rz Axis is moving, then both J3 and J6 Axis will move to compensate the linear movement.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[R3_SCARA_PICK_n_PLACE Routine overview: ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[1. MCTO links the Cartesian XYZRxRyRz and SCARA 4 Axis Robot Coordinate systems (Coordinate Definition for SCARA 4 Axis is J1J2J3J6) and transforms the motion.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[2. MDCC is the master driven speed control instruction that links the Cartesian coordinate system to the virtual master axis for speed override functionality.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[3. MCPM Path move instruction: The Robot is programmed to move to a known Absolute Start Position and then do the ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[   incremental, absolute or with workframe/toolframe offsets incremental moves.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[4. The command tolerance for the first, second and last move is set to 0 units and the third move onwards is set to 20  units for the Pick cycle.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[5. The dynamics of the path move are all programmed in % of max (dyn_data.UnitsMode  is set to 0). ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[6. Turns Counters Example Configuration: To configure the Turns Counters in Absolute Move for Joint J6: set the PathData -> TurnsCounters[2] = - 2 for 2 nos of 360 deg moves]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[7. Joint Command Positions are moved to Tags for visualisation purposes, for HMI/SCADA/OPC.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[R2_JogMaster Routine overview:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[   Jogging the VirtualMaster axis using MAJ instruction will provide the speed override functionality for the Pick and Place cycle.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[See online help 'Configure the SCARA Independent J1J2J3J6 Coordinate System' for more information on configuring 4 Axis SCARA Robots. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[*)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
